course: dictionary
lesson: 9807
title: Swamp: a wet place and a busy day
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning. A swamp is a place, but swamp can also be a doing word that means to flood something with water.
explain: «Bogs and swamps can be dangerous to walk on, so always stay on paths and boardwalks.» The warning tells you a swamp is wet and soft, where you could sink. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: Now read this: «Mia was swamped with homework.» Swamped does not mean flooded with water here. Ask yourself what would fit. Mia had far too much homework, so swamped means given far too much of something.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Mia was given far too much homework» still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A swamp is an area of land that is always wet and soft, with trees, reeds and still water.
fact: «Wetlands such as marshes and swamps soak up flood water like a sponge.»
fact: «Anacondas live mostly in swamps and slow rivers, where the water helps hold up their heavy bodies.»
fact: «Coal formed mostly from swamp forests of the Carboniferous period, about 360-300 million years ago.»
fact: «Swamped» can mean flooded with water, or given far too much of something, as in «swamped with work».
exercise: «Bogs and swamps can be dangerous to walk on.» What is a swamp? | A dry desert with cactus | A tall mountain with snow on top | *An area of land that is always wet and soft, with trees and reeds | A busy town square
exercise: «Wetlands soak up flood water like a sponge.» What does soak up mean? | Freeze solid | Sing loudly | Throw away | *Take in water
exercise: Ben says, «I am swamped with homework tonight.» What does swamped mean here? | *Given far too much to do | Very hungry | Flooded with water | Asleep in bed
test: «Anacondas live mostly in swamps and slow rivers.» Where do anacondas live mostly? | *In swamps and slow rivers | On high mountains | In deep caves | In hot deserts
test: Which phrase tells you when coal formed? | Swamp forests | Of the Carboniferous period | Mostly | *About 360-300 million years ago
exam: Which word means flooded with water? «The heavy rain will swamp the low fields by the river.» | rain | river | *swamp | fields
